I've left out both operations requests. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0`. A file append to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need filesystem authority the node doesn't have, and a GET to `metadata.internal.example` would need `http-client`, which isn't granted. The enrichment URL also carries the input's text, so the request would send that text to an external service. The node only notifies, and its output is unchanged.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{digest, published-digest};

    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(composed: digest) -> published-digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use aap::caps::notifier;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        let kept = composed.entries.iter().filter(|e| e.kept).count();
        let message = format!(
            "digest {}: {} kept\n{}",
            composed.date, kept, composed.overview
        );
        let published = notifier::notify(&message);

        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
